y molecules. This cell maintains cartilage integrity by producing key ECM components and supporting baseline tissue homeostasis. In OA cartilage, this cell is enriched for genes related to cellular homeostasis modulation, including regulation of the cell cycle, development, and RNA metabolism (Ji et al., 2018).\")\n\n  Line 25630: AnnotationAssertion(dc:creator obo:CL_0020020 \"GitHub Copilot\")\n\n  Line 25631: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020020 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\n\n  Line 25632: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37660146\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020020 \"HomC\")\n\n  Line 25633: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020020 \"homeostatic chondrocyte\")\n\n  Line 25634: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020020 obo:CL_0000138)\n\n  Line 25635: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020020 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0070278))\n\n  Line 25636: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020020 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_1990079))\n\n  Line 25638: # Class: obo:CL_0020021 (fibrochondrocyte progenitor cell)\n\n  Line 25640: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36338137\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020021 \"A mesenchymal progenitor cell located in fibrocartilaginous tissues, along the fibrochondrocytic differentiation pathway that co-expresses both fibrochondrocyte markers (COL1A1, COL3A1) and mesenchymal stem cell markers (MCAM/CD146, MYLK) in humans. This cell serves as a progenitor for mature fibrochondrocytes and other meniscal cell types, with differentiation regulated by TGF-β signaling, focal adhesion, and extracellular matrix-receptor interaction pathways.\")\n\n  Line 25641: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020021 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\n\n  Line 25642: AnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020021 \"GitHub Copilot\")\n\n  Line 25643: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation